<text x="213.36" y="48.26" size="5.08" layer="97">Mounting</text>
<text x="88.9" y="2.54" size="1.27" layer="91">Interrupts Available on:  0,1,2,3,7
0 thru 3 fully functional; 7 can do LOW but not CHANGE or FALLING</text>
<text x="2.54" y="147.32" size="1.27" layer="91">5.1K resistors per the spec, allows
uC to sense USB C power advertisement.
(not negotiate - the analog protocol)</text>
<text x="7.62" y="10.16" size="1.27" layer="91" rot="R90">PNP BJT</text>
<text x="238.76" y="154.94" size="1.778" layer="96" rot="MR90">DMP3098L-7</text>
<text x="190.5" y="116.84" size="1.27" layer="91">Coil Active when
DRIVE is HIGH

Use CD40109 to level shift
0 to 5V (uC)  to 0 to 15V (MOSFET)</text>
<text x="25.4" y="2.54" size="1.27" layer="91">555 Timer clears when TRI is LOW
Hence, the TIMER_RST Line is needed since
we cannot use the DRIVE Line (HIGH drives the MOSFET)</text>
<text x="7.62" y="48.26" size="5.08" layer="97">Auto Restart Timer</text>
<wire x1="147.32" y1="55.88" x2="170.18" y2="55.88" width="0.4064" layer="94"/>
<wire x1="170.18" y1="55.88" x2="210.82" y2="55.88" width="0.4064" layer="94"/>
<wire x1="73.66" y1="55.88" x2="73.66" y2="0" width="0.4064" layer="94"/>
<text x="78.74" y="48.26" size="5.08" layer="97">Microcontroller</text>
<wire x1="91.44" y1="121.92" x2="91.44" y2="55.88" width="0.4064" layer="94"/>
<text x="96.52" y="109.22" size="5.08" layer="97">BEMF Measurement</text>
<wire x1="208.28" y1="55.88" x2="208.28" y2="35.56" width="0.4064" layer="94"/>
<wire x1="170.18" y1="114.3" x2="170.18" y2="55.88" width="0.4064" layer="94"/>
<text x="99.06" y="116.84" size="1.778" layer="97">Peak Detector</text>
<text x="93.98" y="58.42" size="1.27" layer="91">Holds Lowest voltage since Reset
Use MOSFET + uC Dio to reset the cap to 5V</text>
<text x="2.54" y="58.42" size="1.27" layer="98">Stage 1:
V+ = (R1*V1 + R2*Vcoil) / (R1 + R2)

Solve for Values by
solving simultaneous equations:
1) Set Coil = 0, choose V+ = 1V (VShift = 2V)
2) Set Coil = 2.69, choose V+ = 1.5V (VShift = 3V)

Solve simultaneously to find that R1 = 4.38 R2.
Choose R2 = 220 (for part unification)
R1 = 50.22k (choose 50k)</text>
<text x="96.52" y="124.46" size="1.27" layer="91">Cascaded Regulators
15V / 500mA for the magnet
5V / 30mA for the ICs</text>
<text x="55.88" y="63.5" size="1.27" layer="98">Stage 2:
VShift = 1 + (R4/R3) V- 
Choose R4=R3=50k (for part unification)
VShift = 2 V-</text>
<text x="66.04" y="76.2" size="1.27" layer="98">Stage 3:
Use spare op-amp
As comparator to DAC voltage
To trigger @ zero crossing.</text>
<text x="7.62" y="43.18" size="1.27" layer="91">TIMER_RESTART will go HIGH after
660k * 4.7uF = 3.1 sec of no pulses.</text>
<text x="139.7" y="91.44" size="1.27" layer="91">PEAK_RESET is DIO
floating (INPUT) 
for normal operation.

OUTPUT HIGH for
at least 5uS for reset.</text>
<text x="139.7" y="66.04" size="1.27" layer="91">0.033uF is an important value
All other caps changed to match
since they are just decoupling.</text>
<text x="114.3" y="99.06" size="1.27" layer="91">Basically any small-signal
shotky should do</text>
<text x="38.1" y="58.42" size="1.016" layer="98">Previous 5V coil operation chose Coil = 1, V+ = 1.5, all resistors 10k.
2.69 b/c the new coil has 2.69 the turns of the old one.</text>
<text x="40.64" y="43.18" size="1.27" layer="91">Use 3x 220k resistors
to use resistor array for easier soldering</text>
<wire x1="195.58" y1="185.42" x2="195.58" y2="167.64" width="0.4064" layer="94"/>
<wire x1="195.58" y1="167.64" x2="185.42" y2="167.64" width="0.4064" layer="94"/>
<wire x1="185.42" y1="167.64" x2="185.42" y2="114.3" width="0.4064" layer="94"/>
<wire x1="185.42" y1="114.3" x2="187.96" y2="114.3" width="0.1524" layer="94"/>
<wire x1="147.32" y1="55.88" x2="147.32" y2="35.56" width="0.4064" layer="94"/>
<text x="160.02" y="48.26" size="5.08" layer="97">Unused</text>
<text x="86.36" y="172.72" size="1.27" layer="91">Special Electrolytic Polymer Cap
Technically vilotes USB 10uF spec,
but experimentally tested ok</text>
